rem Tri-colouring a Triangular Grid
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=189
rem Count the ways to colour the small
rem triangles of a grid of Rows rows in
rem three colours so that triangles that
rem share an edge differ

use linalg
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Rows integer = 8

rem State: the colours u of the up
rem triangles of a row, one tensor axis
rem each. A new row has up colours u and
rem a down triangle between u[i], u[i+1]
rem that must also avoid the up triangle
rem p[i] above it: 3 - |{u[i], u[i+1],
rem p[i]}| choices. Sweep along the row,
rem trading the axis of p[i] for the
rem axis of u[i+1].
Col = array 0 1 2
A = Col reshape 3 1 1
B = Col reshape 1 3 1
C = Col reshape 1 1 3
Diff' = (A not equal B) choose 1 0
Third' = C not equal A and C not equal B
New' = Third choose 1 0
Fac = 3 - (1 + Diff + New)
V = array 1 1 1
for Row in 2 to Rows
  Prev = Row - 1
  W = concat V V V
  for I in 1 to Prev
    Heads = 3 ** I
    Tail = 3 ** (Prev - I)
    Last' = (0 till Heads array) mod 3
    Mat' = Fac Last
    Old' = W reshape Heads 3 Tail
    New' = Mat matmul Old rank 2 2
    Count = Heads * 3 * Tail
    W = New reshape Count
  end
  V = W
end
Answer = V sum
Answer print
